  "body": "## What changed\n\nThe Probe op read the picked feature's placement from the model\n(`model::transform_of`). Generation judges the stylus against the facets\nof the setup frame. In a setup that holds the part turned, the two reads\ndisagreed: the posted cycle sought a surface 10 mm inside the part, with\nno refusal and no diagnostic.\n\n- `operation::probe_pick`: the pick's placement now comes from\n  `setup_align::pose_in(world, entity, setup)`. `probe_seed`,\n  `probe_from_picks` and `probe_account` take `setup: Option<&str>`, the\n  shape #2276 gave the Slot helpers.\n- The call sites pass the operation's setup name:\n  `commands::operation::geometry` (`SetOperationGeometry`),\n  `operation::picks` and `operation::selection_memo`. Both of the last\n  two already had it.\n- `setup_align`: `OpParams::Probe` joins the verified mill kinds\n  (`verified_mill`), so Probe generates on `Mill` and `MillTurn` in an\n  aligned setup. The refusal message now names Probe. Probe is not a\n  turning kind: `verified_turn` is unchanged, and the lathe-post refusal\n  in `lathe_voice` stays.\n- Five sentinels pinned Probe as the refused kind. They now name kinds\n  that are still unverified: a hand-carried `WireContour` params read\n  through `generation_problem` (in the 2D-kinds, multi-axis and\n  op-frame suites), a tilted Contour (the tilted-plane branch in\n  `setup_align`), and the mill-turn loop. The mill-turn suite now\n  asserts Probe is admitted there.\n\n## Readings\n\n- The generation arm already passed setup-frame facets to\n  `probe_op::generate_probe` (the #2210 work). Only the seed read the\n  model frame, so no other generation path needed a change.\n- Probe's `KindInfo` is in `Section::Drilling`, so its family is Mill.\n  One allowlist entry therefore covers `Mill` and `MillTurn`.\n- The overtravel point is not a move: `probing::probe_cycle` records it\n  in `path.probes` only. The moves stop at the tangent point, which is\n  why a seeded touch stays clean while a stale target does not.\n- The stylus law convicts a stale model-frame target because the feed\n  from the safe plane crosses the turned part's top face on the way\n  down.\n\n## Pinning tests\n\n- `setup_align_probe_kinds::turned_probe_reads_its_pick_in_the_setup_frame`\n- `setup_align_probe_kinds::a_model_frame_target_in_a_turned_setup_is_convicted`\n\nNegative control: with the old `model::transform_of` read, the first\ntest fails on the seed (`the turned seed: [20.0, 15.0, 10.0]`) and the\nstylus law convicts that path (`Gouge` at moves 3 to 6). With the fix,\nboth tests pass.\n\n## Not exercised\n\n- No UI change: Probe was refused at generation only, so no ribbon or\n  panel entry was blocked before, and none is blocked now.\n- No MCP change: `set_operation_geometry` calls the same command, so it\n  takes the setup-frame seed with this fix.\n- A pick on a bore, boss, edge or vertex in a turned setup: every mode\n  shares the one placement read that the face proof covers.\n- The `Lathe` and `MillTurn` turning paths, and posts other than the\n  built-in mill post.\n\n## Notes\n\n- The quick gate on this branch has five red binaries unrelated to the\n  change, red at the branch point as well: `example_catalog`,\n  `first_part_programs` and `wire_taper_angle` fail on CRLF checkouts of\n  fixtures and goldens (#2523); `thread_boss` and `thread_mill` fail on\n  stale NC goldens (tool numbers only). Checked: both stay red with the\n  clean `origin/main` code in this same checkout.\n- `crates/app/src/setup_align.rs` is already past the 400-line guide on\n  `main` (457 lines). This change adds one line to it.\n- `SetOperationGeometry::new` and the job-collect region also carry\n  changes in the open PRs #2149 and #2134. A conflict at merge time is\n  expected; this branch takes `origin/main` only at merge time.\n\nChangelog: Probe now generates in a setup that holds the part turned\n(part alignment): its pick seeds the touch on the part as the setup\nholds it, instead of a refusal (#2285).\n\nFixes #2285\n",
